<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24133" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in -tempŏrālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Without time</i>, <i>eternal</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 2, p. 23, 1</span></i>;
			Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ.</span> 10, 316. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Untimely</i>, <i>unseasonable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Acut. 2, 10</span></i>
			.— <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intempŏrālĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>unseasonably</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uti cataplasmatibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 1, 9, 50</span></i>
			.</div>
